Breya is not just an artifact value engine; she is an infinite mana sink and sacrifice payoff sitting in the command zone. The single biggest mistake a new pilot makes is casting Breya on curve without protection or an active loop ready. Her true strength is assembling Ashnod's Altar or Krark-Clan Ironworks alongside Nim Deathmantle or Eldrazi Displacer, then deploying Breya to immediately close the game in a single turn.
Bracket 3: the Game Changer cap is three, filled by Cyclonic Rift, Demonic Tutor, and The One Ring. No mass land denial. Infinite combo lines assemble turns 5–6 and execute from turn 6 onward.

# The core loops
Breya, Etherium Shaper + Nim Deathmantle + Ashnod's Altar :: sacrifice two Thopters to the Altar for four mana, then sacrifice Breya for two mana; pay four into Deathmantle's trigger to return Breya with two fresh Thopters, netting two colorless mana per loop. Repeat for infinite colorless mana and infinite Thopters, then spend the mana and Thopters into Breya's ability to deal infinite damage to all opponents.
Breya, Etherium Shaper + Nim Deathmantle + Krark-Clan Ironworks :: operates identically to the Altar loop because Breya and her Thopter tokens are all artifacts, sacrificing to KCI for two mana each. Generates infinite colorless mana, infinite tokens, and infinite Breya damage.
Breya, Etherium Shaper + Eldrazi Displacer + Ashnod's Altar :: sacrifice two Thopters to the Altar for four mana, then pay three mana to activate Displacer flickering Breya; Breya returns with two fresh Thopters, netting one colorless mana per loop. Repeat for infinite colorless mana, infinite Thopters, and infinite Breya damage.
Breya, Etherium Shaper + Eldrazi Displacer + Krark-Clan Ironworks :: identical to the Displacer-Altar loop using KCI as the sacrifice outlet.
Thopter Foundry + Sword of the Meek + Ashnod's Altar :: pay one to sacrifice Sword to Foundry, creating a 1/1 Thopter and gaining one life; Sword triggers on the 1/1 entering and returns attached to it; sacrifice the Thopter to Altar for two mana. Net one mana and one life per repetition for infinite mana, infinite life, and infinite Thopters.
Thopter Foundry + Sword of the Meek + Time Sieve :: pay five mana into Thopter Foundry to create five Thopters while recurring Sword of the Meek; tap Time Sieve and sacrifice the five Thopters to take an extra turn. Repeat every turn for infinite turns.
Sensei's Divining Top + Mystic Forge + Etherium Sculptor :: with Sculptor reducing Top's cost to zero, tap Top to draw a card and put it on top of your library; cast Top for free from your library with Mystic Forge. Repeat to draw your entire deck and assemble any winning line.

# Artifact tutors and lines
Trophy Mage -> Ashnod's Altar :: searches specifically for the 3-CMC sacrifice engine directly to hand
Tribute Mage -> Nim Deathmantle :: searches for the 2-CMC recursion engine to hand
Tribute Mage -> Thopter Foundry :: searches for the token creation half of the Sword loop
Tribute Mage -> Time Sieve :: searches for the extra-turn engine when Thopter Foundry and Sword of the Meek are assembled
Tribute Mage -> Wishclaw Talisman :: finds an unconditional tutor on a 2-CMC artifact body
Fabricate -> Nim Deathmantle :: universal artifact tutor to hand to complete whatever combo half is missing
Whir of Invention -> Krark-Clan Ironworks :: instant-speed tutor using improvise to put KCI directly onto the battlefield on an opponent's end step
Reshape -> Ashnod's Altar :: sacrifices an expendable Thopter token to drop the Altar straight into play
Beseech the Mirror -> Ashnod's Altar :: bargain a Thopter token to search and cast the Altar directly onto the battlefield for free
Goblin Engineer -> Nim Deathmantle :: entombs Deathmantle directly to your graveyard, then taps to sacrifice a Thopter and return it to play
Goblin Welder :: swaps spent mana rocks or Thopters in play for counterspelled or discarded combo pieces in your graveyard
Demonic Tutor -> Ashnod's Altar :: unconditional two-mana tutor for whichever piece completes your winning line
Tezzeret the Seeker :: untaps two mana rocks to accelerate, or searches any combo piece directly onto the battlefield
Inventors' Fair -> Ashnod's Altar :: once metalcraft is active, sacrifice the land to fetch the missing combo engine
Urza's Saga -> Sol Ring :: early explosive mana acceleration on Chapter III before the land sacrifices itself
Urza's Saga -> Skullclamp :: finds the primary draw engine to turn Breya's Thopters into raw cards

# Mana and engine velocity
Sol Ring + Arcane Signet + Fellwar Stone :: reliable low-cost acceleration that fixes Breya's four-color requirement
Mox Opal + Lotus Petal :: zero-mana artifact acceleration that triggers metalcraft and enables explosive early turns
Etherium Sculptor + Enthusiastic Mechanaut + Foundry Inspector :: cost reducers that make casting multiple artifacts effortless and enable the Top-Forge loop
Lotho, Corrupt Shirriff :: produces artifact Treasures whenever players cast two spells in a turn, feeding metalcraft and sacrifice outlets
Emry, Lurker of the Loch :: self-mills to fill the graveyard with artifact targets and casts them repeatedly
Sai, Master Thopterist :: creates flying Thopters whenever you cast an artifact, providing endless sacrifice fodder for Altar and KCI
Jhoira, Weatherlight Captain :: draws a card for every historic spell cast, storming through your library as you deploy rocks and combo pieces
The One Ring :: grants protection from everything for a turn while drawing deep into your combo pieces and free interaction
Mystic Remora + Esper Sentinel :: early game taxes that draw cards off opposing development
Skullclamp :: attach to 1/1 Thopters to draw two cards for one mana, digging rapidly toward missing tutors

# Payoffs and life loss
Marionette Apprentice :: drains each opponent for one life whenever any artifact or creature you control is put into a graveyard, converting sacrifice loops into an immediate table kill without needing combat
Marionette Master :: with fabricate 3, each sacrificed artifact drains an opponent for four life; sacrificing five artifacts to Time Sieve or KCI deletes a player instantly
Padeem, Consul of Innovation :: grants hexproof to all your artifacts, completely insulating Ashnod's Altar, Nim Deathmantle, and KCI from targeted removal

# Interaction and protection
Grand Abolisher :: completely silences opposing interaction and activated abilities on your winning combo turn
Silence :: one white mana on your upkeep or main phase to prevent opponents from casting spells during your combo attempt
Deflecting Swat :: zero-mana redirect while Breya is on the battlefield, protecting your combo pieces from exile or destruction
Pact of Negation + Force of Negation :: zero-mana counterspells to ensure your winning line resolves through opposing countermagic
Mana Drain + Counterspell + Dovin's Veto :: efficient hard counterspells that stop opposing game-winning plays or protect your setup
Dispatch :: one-mana instant exile with metalcraft active, removing any creature threat with zero drawbacks
Swords to Plowshares :: unconditional one-mana spot exile
Toxic Deluge :: low-cost sweeper to reset aggressive creature boards while leaving your mana rocks intact
Cyclonic Rift :: instant-speed overloaded reset that clears opposing blockers and disruptive stax pieces
Sevinne's Reclamation :: recovers up to three destroyed or milled combo pieces from your graveyard across two casts

# What to keep and sequencing
A functional opening hand requires three lands or two lands with a mana rock (Sol Ring, Signet, Talisman), access to blue and black mana, and either a tutor (Tribute Mage, Fabricate, Goblin Engineer) or an early draw engine (Mystic Remora, Esper Sentinel, Skullclamp). Never keep hands with four colors of lands but zero plays before turn four.
Spend turns 1 through 3 deploying mana rocks, establishing cost reducers, and accumulating Thopter fodder with Sai or Lotho.
Do not run Breya out onto an empty board without purpose; she is your finisher. Use your tutors to locate Nim Deathmantle and Ashnod's Altar (or KCI).
When ready to combo on turn 6 or later, lead with Silence or Grand Abolisher to lock opponents out of interaction. Cast your sacrifice outlet and Deathmantle first, then cast Breya and execute the infinite loop in response to her enter-the-battlefield trigger.
